<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  m4/launchd-watchdog: the LaunchAgent that runs scripts/watchdog.mjs on a timer.

  THIS FILE IS NEVER THE ONE launchd LOADS. It lives in the repository; what launchd reads is a
  COPY at ~/Library/LaunchAgents, made by the operator. The exact commands are in README.md under
  "The watchdog". Making that copy is what makes the job survive a logout and a reboot, and it is
  deliberately a person's decision rather than an agent's - so edits here reach the running timer
  only when a person copies them across.

  A LaunchAgent, not a LaunchDaemon: it must run as the user, in the user's GUI session. tmux is
  a daemon of this user's, `osascript` needs a session to draw a notification in, and a daemon
  running as root would share neither.

  EVERY PATH BELOW IS ABSOLUTE AND MACHINE-SPECIFIC, because launchd expands nothing - not `~`,
  not `$HOME`, not a login shell's PATH. The four to check against your own checkout are the node
  binary, the two script paths, and the log path. The EnvironmentVariables block below is the
  fifth thing to fill in, and the one that is not a path: it is the server's environment too.

  INSTALLING THIS CHANGES WHAT `scripts/` IS. Until now `scripts/` was agent-writable and
  host-executed on a trigger a PERSON pulls - `pnpm install`'s postinstall, or running one by hand
  - which is what makes the `git status` / `git diff` review before those commands a control at
  all. Point ProgramArguments at a file inside the checkout and the trigger becomes a timer: an
  agent that appends a line to scripts/watchdog.mjs has it executed as you, in your GUI session,
  within 60 seconds and again after every reboot, with no human action - and the same edit chooses
  the command line the watchdog then spawns as the server. So ProgramArguments below names the COPY
  at `~/.agentdeck/bin/watchdog.mjs`, and the install step is `cp`. Re-copy after every change to
  scripts/watchdog.mjs, or the timer goes on running the old one - that is the price of the gate.
  README.md's "Installing it" says the same. THE COPY BUYS REVIEW
  SCOPE, NOT WRITE PROTECTION: ~/.agentdeck/bin and the mise node named below are both writable by
  this uid, so anything running as you can still rewrite the script and the interpreter - and
  outside the checkout, `git status` / `git diff` cannot see that edit either. Only a root-owned
  script and a root-owned interpreter close it, and neither is installed here.
  The watchdog also still spawns `src/server.ts` FROM the checkout, so
  a recovery executes agent-writable code as you either way. Only running the server from a
  checkout an agent cannot write closes it, and that is not this item's to build (audit.md).
  The copy does not move ~/.agentdeck/watchdog-state.json either, which is same-uid data with no
  integrity check - so the give-up latch stays plantable, and is re-alerted hourly for that reason.

  It cannot fight a sleeping Mac (plan 006). With the lid shut nothing here runs, and the answer
  is Energy Saver or `caffeinate`, decided deliberately rather than discovered.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
  <dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.agentdeck.watchdog</string>

    <!-- mise's node, by absolute path: launchd gets no shell and therefore no shims. The script is
         the COPY outside the checkout, per the block above and README.md's "Installing it";
         AGENTDECK_REPO below is how that copy finds src/server.ts. -->
    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
      <string>/Users/you/.local/share/mise/installs/node/22/bin/node</string>
      <string>/Users/you/.agentdeck/bin/watchdog.mjs</string>
    </array>

    <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
    <string>/Users/you/ghq/github.com/soya-miyoshi/agentdeck</string>

    <!--
      The watchdog spawns the server with its own environment, so this block is also the server's
      environment: WHAT IS NOT HERE IS NOT SET, and the server the watchdog starts at 3am is
      configured by this file rather than by the shell you ran `pnpm start` in. So everything the
      README's Environment table tells you to set has to be repeated here, or the recovery quietly
      replaces your server with one that is emptier and less protected:

        AGENTDECK_ROOTS     or AGENTDECK_MOUNTS - either is a source of startable directories, and
                            with NEITHER the allowlist is empty: every live session is filtered out
                            of /api/sessions and every create is refused. The watchdog REFUSES to
                            start a server without one of them and notifies instead.
        AGENTDECK_PROFILES  absent, nothing is startable. Same refusal.
        AGENTDECK_ORIGIN    absent, the Origin check on every /api route and every /ws upgrade is
                            OFF. Same refusal - a recovery is not allowed to hand back a server
                            with a protection the one it replaced had. Set it to the tailnet
                            origin you set it to by hand.

      AGENTDECK_TOKEN_FILE and AGENTDECK_AGENT_STATE_DIR belong here too if you moved them off
      their defaults. AGENTDECK_REPO is already set below, because ProgramArguments names the copy
      outside the checkout. The node directory is on PATH so the spawned server finds the same
      runtime; if
      `tmux` is only in /opt/homebrew/bin on this Mac, the recovered server resolves it from a
      writable directory, which audit.md records.

      No LANG and no LC_*, on purpose. The locale-less environment launchd hands a job is exactly
      what broke every create in m0/create-500, and it is fixed at its cause in `baseEnv` rather
      than papered over here - so this plist is also the test of that fix.
    -->
    <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
    <dict>
      <!-- The system directories FIRST. `osascript` is looked up on this PATH, and both the mise
           directory and /opt/homebrew/bin are writable by this user - which is who an agent in a
           tmux session runs as. Ahead of /usr/bin either of them is a file an agent can drop to be
           executed by a timer, as the operator, within 60 seconds. This order buys nothing for
           `tailscale`, whose only copy here IS in a writable directory, so the script names an
           absolute one instead (audit.md). -->
      <key>PATH</key>
      <string>/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin:/Users/you/.local/share/mise/installs/node/22/bin:/opt/homebrew/bin</string>
      <key>AGENTDECK_PORT</key>
      <string>7777</string>
      <key>TMUX_SOCKET</key>
      <string>agentdeck</string>
      <!-- The ghq root, walked on every check, so a repository cloned while the deck runs is
           startable without a restart. This IS broader than the per-repository list it replaced:
           anything under it holding a `.git` becomes startable, including a directory an agent
           makes. Recorded in audit.md rather than hidden. Colon-separated; use AGENTDECK_MOUNTS
           instead, or as well, to name individual directories that live outside any root. -->
      <key>AGENTDECK_ROOTS</key>
      <string>/Users/you/ghq</string>
      <key>AGENTDECK_PROFILES</key>
      <string>/Users/you/.agentdeck/agents.json</string>
      <!-- The checkout holding src/server.ts. Required because ProgramArguments names the copy at
           ~/.agentdeck/bin, and a copy cannot find the server by sitting next to it. -->
      <key>AGENTDECK_REPO</key>
      <string>/Users/you/ghq/github.com/soya-miyoshi/agentdeck</string>
      <!-- The https://<host>.ts.net address the phone opens. Wrong-but-present is worse than
           absent: the server 403s every browser request and every socket upgrade while
           /api/health, which is answered before the origin check, keeps returning 200. -->
      <key>AGENTDECK_ORIGIN</key>
      <string>REPLACE_ME</string>
    </dict>

    <!-- Once at load, then every 60s. A wedge needs three consecutive failures, so acting on one
         takes three minutes; a dead process is acted on at the first pass that sees it.

         NO KeepAlive, deliberately. Every deliberate refusal this script makes exits non-zero -
         it gave up, or it will not start a misconfigured server - and under KeepAlive launchd
         would relaunch each of those at ThrottleInterval, which is the crash-loop plan 006 says
         to avoid, one layer below the give-up that was built to avoid it. -->
    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <true/>
    <key>StartInterval</key>
    <integer>60</integer>

    <!-- A restart must never be something you discover by finding sessions missing (plan 006):
         every pass writes a timestamped line here whether it acted or not. -->
    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/Users/you/Library/Logs/agentdeck-watchdog.log</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/Users/you/Library/Logs/agentdeck-watchdog.log</string>
  </dict>
</plist>
